      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Idanha%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Idanha's name was adopted from a mineral-water brand bottled in Soda Springs, Idaho.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Idanha%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Railroad workers and loggers established a small town here by 1891 to connect the Willamette Valley to Eastern Oregon.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
